A||||2||Eric||Removing door skin
Z||000000||Eric||07-07-99||04:19 PM||||Could someone tell me how to remove the outer door panel?  I took out all the torx bolts that look like they are holding the door together and it still won't budge.  I'm trying to get to the power window motor and throught the outside looks like the easiest way.
Z||000001||GREENDANO||07-07-99||07:37 PM||||Eric,<br>  To get the door skin off, the easiest thing to do is remove the inner door panel.  Take the mirror off, and disconnect most of the linkages.  So it looks as if you should leave the skin on and save yourself from potential paint damage.<br>  I'm sure someone has done this without removing the door panel, I'm just telling you the easiest way.  Plus it's not that hard to remove the interior door panel.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000002||ChadMan||07-08-99||07:02 AM||||In addition to the torx bolts and the mirror, there are two (7 mm?) bolts underneath the black molding that runs along the door.  If you can get the black molding off without breaking the white clips that hold it in place, you're a more patient man than I am.<br>
